WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:01.550
Death.

00:00:01.550 --> 00:00:05.750
That terrible and inevitable consequence of
life.

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:11.160
But as the Foundation discovered in the aftermath
of Project Dammerung, its absence can be even

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:13.519
more horrifying than its presence.

00:00:13.519 --> 00:00:15.950
Let’s bring you up to speed, shall we?

00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:22.640
Here’s the story so far: After the death
of overseer O5-11, the SCP Foundation’s

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:28.349
infamous O5 Council learned the horrifying
truth of what happens to human beings after

00:00:28.349 --> 00:00:29.349
death.

00:00:29.349 --> 00:00:35.410
There’s no afterlife, no everlasting paradise
or eternal damnation.

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:41.920
Instead, the dead are cursed to remain conscious,
aware of everything happening to them after

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:45.490
passing… even their bodies decomposing.

00:00:45.490 --> 00:00:51.060
To combat this, a member of the council, O5-4,
established Project Dammerung.

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:56.870
This was an internal, Foundation-backed endeavor,
created with one singular goal in mind: to

00:00:56.870 --> 00:00:59.870
capture and contain death itself.

00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:04.160
As part of this project, researchers created
a machine known as SCP-3448.

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:11.219
At first, it seemed like just an ordinary
MRI machine from a hospital, SCP-3448 had

00:01:11.219 --> 00:01:17.329
a number of anomalous modifications made to
it, giving it a rather unique function.

00:01:17.329 --> 00:01:21.880
The device was capable of separating someone’s
consciousness from their body, putting them

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:23.560
in a sort of half-dead state.

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:30.229
While in this state, a subject placed within
the machine, referred to as SCP-3448-A, could

00:01:30.229 --> 00:01:35.409
maintain a consistent line of two-way communication
between their disembodied consciousness and

00:01:35.409 --> 00:01:36.840
the Foundation.

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:42.210
Instead of deploying a member of D-Class personnel,
one of the SCP Foundation’s own agents was

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:45.189
placed into SCP-3448.

00:01:45.189 --> 00:01:52.770
Agent Anthony Michaels was elected to act
as SCP-3448-A, and serve as the conduit between

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:56.189
the living world and the endless nothing that
lies beyond.

00:01:56.189 --> 00:02:03.179
But, as often happens when people dabble with
forces they cannot possibly understand, something

00:02:03.179 --> 00:02:04.849
went awry.

00:02:04.849 --> 00:02:09.259
Project Dammerung’s mission to contain death
took an unexpected turn.

00:02:09.259 --> 00:02:15.190
When Agent Michaels was placed into the machine,
things ended up getting much, much worse.

00:02:15.190 --> 00:02:19.700
Buckle up, because we’re about to dive into
the ill-fated outcome of the death-defying

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:24.620
Project Dammerung, the catalyst for the End
of Death itself.

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:29.000
One of the components connected to SCP-3448
is a monitor.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:34.680
This screen is used to interpret the electrical
activity of SCP-3448-A’s brain once they

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:40.420
have entered the half-death state, known as
SCP-3448-1.

00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:45.370
This component of the anomalous MRI machine
is able to intake these electrical signals

00:02:45.370 --> 00:02:50.650
and interpret them as images, occasionally
with words accompanying them too.

00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:55.120
During his time in the machine, Agent Michaels’
brainwaves were able to deliver some rather

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:58.180
interesting imagery to the Foundation researchers.

00:02:58.180 --> 00:03:03.400
A number of these seemed to be a bizarre and
seemingly disconnected series of images, almost

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:08.490
like something taken directly out of a dream,
hard to find any real context for.

00:03:08.490 --> 00:03:13.370
The first was a human figure, surrounded by
a swarm of buzzing insects.

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:19.350
After forty-three minutes, the monitor connected
to SCP-3448 showed this figure looking swollen

00:03:19.350 --> 00:03:25.150
as if it had been stung by the insects, which
flew away as the obscured humanoid collapsed.

00:03:25.150 --> 00:03:30.180
The next day, the screen showed a man lying
alone in a desert somewhere, with an oasis

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:35.350
in the distance; almost like the classic mirage
someone dying of thirst sees just out of reach

00:03:35.350 --> 00:03:38.350
as they stumble through the endless sand dunes.

00:03:38.350 --> 00:03:43.630
The same day, the image changed to a man in
a fetal position, in a room made of dirt,

00:03:43.630 --> 00:03:46.630
with bones and roots protruding from the walls.

00:03:46.630 --> 00:03:51.650
So far, the dream-like images coming through
from Agent Michaels’ half-dead mind look

00:03:51.650 --> 00:03:57.310
strange, almost like the contents of the infamous
videotape from the horror movie The Ring.

00:03:57.310 --> 00:03:59.990
Did any of these images mean anything?

00:03:59.990 --> 00:04:01.890
And if so, what?

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:06.840
Was the man - the human-shaped figure appearing
in them - Agent Michaels himself, or some

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:12.080
kind of representation of his disembodied
consciousness, now that it had been separated

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:15.900
from him by the SCP-3448 machine?

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:20.240
One of the Foundation’s researchers described
the imagery seen on the monitor as being akin

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:23.490
to watching someone’s acid trip for over
a week.

00:04:23.490 --> 00:04:28.410
However, the same researcher also theorized
that, because Agent Michaels was being held

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:33.460
in a half-dead state, that the other things
appearing in the images with him could also

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:35.780
be similarly half-dead.

00:04:35.780 --> 00:04:40.060
The researcher believed that what they were
seeing was more of an abstract, conceptual

00:04:40.060 --> 00:04:46.040
representation of death, not a conventional
afterlife, like the idea of walking up to

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:49.310
the pearly gates, or the fire and brimstone
of Hell.

00:04:49.310 --> 00:04:55.000
So, the researcher decided to try ‘half-killing’
objects, partially disassembling things and

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:59.290
placing them into SCP-3448 with Agent Michaels.

00:04:59.290 --> 00:05:03.710
Sure enough, doing this meant that the man
in the images now had whatever object was

00:05:03.710 --> 00:05:08.060
put into the machine; for example, when they
broke apart a lighter, it appeared in the

00:05:08.060 --> 00:05:10.639
man’s possession on-screen.

00:05:10.639 --> 00:05:14.640
Unfortunately, this was the biggest mistake
that the researcher could have made.

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:19.870
The images on the monitor began to show the
man, now believed to be Agent Anthony Michaels,

00:05:19.870 --> 00:05:21.960
being attacked by a little girl.

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:26.770
Thought to be a manifestation of the very
concept of death, this girl was seen stabbing

00:05:26.770 --> 00:05:32.180
the agent with a femur, torturing him while
the Foundation were sat watching, powerless

00:05:32.180 --> 00:05:34.370
and unable to help.

00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:39.020
The researcher requisitioned a handgun, partially
disassembling it like the lighter in order

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:42.180
to arm Agent Michaels against his attacker.

00:05:42.180 --> 00:05:43.270
And it worked.

00:05:43.270 --> 00:05:46.220
But the consequences were unfathomable.

00:05:46.220 --> 00:05:50.600
Sure enough, Michaels was able to draw the
firearm and fend off his attacker.

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:55.590
The agent fired off a shot that, over the
course of more bizarre, creepy, and disjointed

00:05:55.590 --> 00:06:01.540
images involving skeletons and teddy bears,
seemed to hit the girl square in the head.

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:06.230
The image that followed showed Agent Michaels
standing alone in a garden, flowers blooming

00:06:06.230 --> 00:06:09.460
as dead insects rained down around him.

00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:14.230
On the ground beside the agent was a stuffed
animal, a crow with a bullet hole through

00:06:14.230 --> 00:06:15.320
its head.

00:06:15.320 --> 00:06:20.720
Shortly after, the following words appeared
on the monitor attached to SCP-3448: “I

00:06:20.720 --> 00:06:23.390
hope you enjoy your hike, dad.”

00:06:23.390 --> 00:06:27.070
For a few short moments, nothing seemed to
be all that different to the Foundation in

00:06:27.070 --> 00:06:28.440
the outside world.

00:06:28.440 --> 00:06:32.510
The researcher who had provided Agent Michaels
with the handgun was trapped in a state of

00:06:32.510 --> 00:06:37.250
shock for a brief while, until five minutes
later when the phone calls started flooding

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:38.250
in.

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:42.540
The first came from Joyce, a woman known to
the researcher, who frantically explained

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:47.170
how her father – who had been dying – now
was totally fine all of a sudden.

00:06:47.170 --> 00:06:51.680
The researcher couldn’t quite tell if she
was happy or terrified by what seemed to be

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:52.680
happening.

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:54.330
Next came the orders from above.

00:06:54.330 --> 00:06:59.650
The overseer, O5-4, the only council member
aware of Project Dammerung and who had backed

00:06:59.650 --> 00:07:04.270
it financially, called to congratulate the
researcher and the rest of the team behind

00:07:04.270 --> 00:07:05.270
the project.

00:07:05.270 --> 00:07:09.990
It seemed that Dammerung had been successful
in the goal they had set out with, to contain

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:12.800
the cognitohazard known as death.

00:07:12.800 --> 00:07:18.640
O5-4 demanded that all records and information
regarding the project was to be incinerated,

00:07:18.640 --> 00:07:21.580
covered up from the rest of the Foundation’s
knowledge.

00:07:21.580 --> 00:07:26.120
But the truth was far, far worse than any
at the Foundation realized.

00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:30.240
It soon dawned on the researcher, who had
been documenting Agent Michaels’ time in

00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:35.199
SCP-3448, that Project Dammerung had not succeeded
at all.

00:07:35.199 --> 00:07:40.260
They hadn’t contained anything, hadn’t
secured the conceptual form of death.

00:07:40.260 --> 00:07:45.990
What they had done instead, by foolish mistake,
was neutralize death.

00:07:45.990 --> 00:07:48.669
They had killed death itself.

00:07:48.669 --> 00:07:53.410
And now, the world as they knew it was gone,
changed almost indefinitely.

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:57.259
Now, not a single person in the world could
die.

00:07:57.259 --> 00:08:00.900
They had caused the End of Death.

00:08:00.900 --> 00:08:06.090
On the surface, a world without death sounds
like a utopia, a blissful society where everyone

00:08:06.090 --> 00:08:09.010
on Earth lives a long and prosperous life.

00:08:09.010 --> 00:08:13.120
But those with a little more foresight will
know that peaceful immortality for the human

00:08:13.120 --> 00:08:15.300
race is a fool’s dream.

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:18.560
Think about how many people there are living
in the world right now.

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:22.199
The overall global population grows exponentially
every year.

00:08:22.199 --> 00:08:28.389
While death might be a sad and somber part
of life, it’s unfortunately necessary.

00:08:28.389 --> 00:08:32.830
Even with all the deaths that occur worldwide
every year, the resources of Planet Earth

00:08:32.830 --> 00:08:35.180
are still being stretched thin.

00:08:35.180 --> 00:08:41.729
Water, oil, food, electricity, homes, everywhere
you go there are plenty of people who don’t

00:08:41.729 --> 00:08:42.760
have enough of any.

00:08:42.760 --> 00:08:47.980
So, what happens when people don’t die,
just keep aging infinitely?

00:08:47.980 --> 00:08:52.990
What happens when the Earth becomes too overcrowded,
when the number of people overshadows the

00:08:52.990 --> 00:08:57.510
number of resources even more than it already
does?

00:08:57.510 --> 00:09:01.730
Society as we know it, across the globe, would
collapse.

00:09:01.730 --> 00:09:03.690
And that’s exactly what happened.

00:09:03.690 --> 00:09:08.540
The Foundation had done the unthinkable, they
had vanquished the very concept that takes

00:09:08.540 --> 00:09:10.800
us from being alive to being deceased.

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:17.820
But there’s a reason Kilroy J. Oldster called
death “the great equalizer of human beings.”

00:09:17.820 --> 00:09:23.960
It is meant to catch up with everyone, every
person born is ultimately destined to die.

00:09:23.960 --> 00:09:29.510
And by removing that element of human mortality
from the equation, the SCP Foundation had

00:09:29.510 --> 00:09:33.300
unknowingly pushed the world towards disaster.

00:09:33.300 --> 00:09:40.420
With the actions of Agent Michaels within
SCP-3448, death as a concept ceased to exist,

00:09:40.420 --> 00:09:45.320
almost instantaneously as if someone had flipped
an off switch.

00:09:45.320 --> 00:09:50.630
People didn’t become undead, things that
had long since passed away and been confined

00:09:50.630 --> 00:09:55.050
to six feet under the dirt didn’t start
clawing their way back up to the surface.

00:09:55.050 --> 00:09:59.600
We aren’t talking about a zombie outbreak;
this isn’t Dawn of the Dead.

00:09:59.600 --> 00:10:05.300
Instead, human beings across the world just
refused to die, their brains continuing to

00:10:05.300 --> 00:10:11.300
function and bodies continuing to age, despite
any damage or injuries they sustained.

00:10:11.300 --> 00:10:16.540
Fatal wounds were now just as dangerous as
getting a broken ankle or sprained wrist.

00:10:16.540 --> 00:10:21.110
The concerns around how undying humans were
overpopulating the planet were also extended

00:10:21.110 --> 00:10:26.270
to animals too, which were also affected by
the End of Death that Project Dammerung had

00:10:26.270 --> 00:10:27.270
triggered.

00:10:27.270 --> 00:10:31.190
As a result, the threat of starvation on a
potentially global scale was greater than

00:10:31.190 --> 00:10:33.570
such a concern ever had been.

00:10:33.570 --> 00:10:38.640
Of course, the SCP Foundation left the concerns
of a potential humanitarian crisis to those

00:10:38.640 --> 00:10:40.740
in charge of world governments.

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:44.610
The United Nations could worry themselves
over how to feed and care for a population

00:10:44.610 --> 00:10:49.190
that simply won’t die, the Foundation had
bigger fish to fry.

00:10:49.190 --> 00:10:53.830
Their mistake had caused this situation, so
only they could undo it.

00:10:53.830 --> 00:10:56.149
The only solution they could come up with?

00:10:56.149 --> 00:10:58.860
Figuring out new ways of killing people.

00:10:58.860 --> 00:11:02.149
The Foundation wanted to bring death back
to the dead.

00:11:02.149 --> 00:11:07.020
Their experiments began with the use of D-Class
personnel, commanding them to attempt to kill

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:09.490
one another through various means.

00:11:09.490 --> 00:11:13.740
Strangulation, both by hand or with the use
of a belt, didn’t seem to work the way it

00:11:13.740 --> 00:11:18.520
should have, with the D-Class being strangled,
likely going into a coma due to a lack of

00:11:18.520 --> 00:11:20.450
oxygen to their brain.

00:11:20.450 --> 00:11:24.399
Not dying, but living in unconscious agony.

00:11:24.399 --> 00:11:29.370
In a similar experiment, placing a D-Class
in a vacuum led to burst blood vessels, impaired

00:11:29.370 --> 00:11:33.610
motor functions, widespread paralysis to name
a few forms of damage.

00:11:33.610 --> 00:11:35.970
But still, death could not be achieved.

00:11:35.970 --> 00:11:42.110
Cutting, blood loss, poisoning, starvation,
shooting, even decapitation of multiple D-Class

00:11:42.110 --> 00:11:44.870
personnel all yielded the same result.

00:11:44.870 --> 00:11:49.990
In some sense, simply allowing these subjects
to die might have just been kinder; if death

00:11:49.990 --> 00:11:52.420
was still possible, that is.

00:11:52.420 --> 00:11:56.769
The Foundation even went as far as removing
the brain of a live monkey, placing it in

00:11:56.769 --> 00:12:01.410
a blender and testing to see if there was
any electrical activity present.

00:12:01.410 --> 00:12:08.090
And wouldn’t you know, it was somehow still
alive, at least as far as life can be measured

00:12:08.090 --> 00:12:09.910
by human beings.

00:12:09.910 --> 00:12:16.520
This key part of our existence, the underlying
fact of death itself, was no more.

00:12:16.520 --> 00:12:21.220
Removing that was like taking a crucial element
out of a circuit, the world just didn’t

00:12:21.220 --> 00:12:24.810
function in the way it was supposed to anymore.

00:12:24.810 --> 00:12:27.220
What hope did the Foundation have now?

00:12:27.220 --> 00:12:30.769
What could possibly be done to solve this
colossal mistake?

00:12:30.769 --> 00:12:37.040
Well, the answer is very little, apart from
waiting for the inevitable collapse of society.

00:12:37.040 --> 00:12:42.519
What awaited was a world in ruin where everyone
was starving but nobody could die.

00:12:42.519 --> 00:12:49.430
A planet and a people just hanging on until
the universe eventually blinked out of existence,

00:12:49.430 --> 00:12:53.640
so that maybe then they could Rest in Peace.

00:12:53.640 --> 00:12:54.800
The moral of the story?

00:12:54.800 --> 00:13:02.120
You can’t cheat death, because death isn’t
the other player, it’s the game itself.

00:13:02.120 --> 00:13:07.399
Now go check out “Secret Group that Runs
the World - SCP O5 Council Explained” and

00:13:07.399 --> 00:13:12.620
“SCP-006 - Fountain of Youth” for more
videos about attempts to cheat death, and

00:13:12.620 --> 00:13:14.490
its not-so-pleasant consequences!

